ep-finder authors

Karol Bartkiewicz <bark@amu.edu.pl> (maintainer)
  Faculty of Physics and Astronomy, Adam Mickiewicz University, Poznan, Poland
  Conceived the idea and developed the theory of the article, including Lemma 1, Theorem 1 and
  their consequences, carried out the link-model and programming calculations, and wrote the
  manuscript. Maintains this repository.

Hubert Wojewoda
  Faculty of Physics and Astronomy, Adam Mickiewicz University, Poznan, Poland
  Developed and validated the numerical search for exceptional points in the ep-finder code
  (ep_finder/), including the Gaussian-process-guided octree, and mapped the EP manifolds of the
  ring and of the Perina two-mode model.

Franco Nori
  RIKEN, Wako-shi, Saitama, Japan, and Department of Physics, University of Michigan, Ann Arbor, USA
  Took part in the scientific discussions and helped to prepare the manuscript.
